Third-party software
--------------------

The jsq and vrotdaem binaries are built from Rust crates and C libraries that
keep their own licenses, among them SQLite (public domain), Zstandard
(BSD-3-Clause) and crates under the MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause,
BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Zlib, Unicode-3.0 and CDLA-Permissive-2.0 licenses. Every
release archive carries a THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES file with the full license text
of each of them and the crates it covers. In a source checkout the same file
is produced by running:

    cargo about generate about.hbs -o THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES

Every dependency and its exact version is listed in Cargo.lock.
